Z||000002||jch82||04-08-2001||10:28 PM||||MooCow has the 4:10 with a 3.4 and it definitely has more oomph than the M17. Even if you only refresh the 2.8, I would still go with the M19 because it is geared lower and will have more low end. Just my thoughts  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Yeah, my girlfriend takes collect calls from the road<BR>And it doesn't seem to matter that I'm lacking in the bulge<BR>She laughs at my dumb jokes when no one does<BR>She brings me mexican food from Sombrero's just because<BR>                 <I>-Blink 182</I>||||reg||12
Z||000003||WKDFIRO||04-09-2001||04:21 AM||||If for a little oomph and all around performance I would go 3.1 with the 3.65. <P>The 4.10 is a killer on the freeway and even at the speed limit will guzzle gas before you know it! <P>Careful, sometimes "refreshing" the engine leads on to bigger things...I remember when I just wanted to "freshen" up my 2.8....<P>Before I know it I got a laundry list of upgrades just because of the motor mantra - "I have it out I might as well..."||||reg||12
Z||000004||1FST2M6||04-09-2001||08:15 AM||||4:!0 and a nice shot of nitrous!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> i loved mine! and GT Bastard is picking fights with it all time! ||||reg||1
Z||000005||jch82||04-09-2001||09:59 AM||||Ken only runs at about 3200-3500 highway speed with the 4:10 tranny. That isn't to bad I don't think. He drove it all the way from The Fiero Factory to Muskegon, MI (700mi trip) at highway speed. It handled just fine....<P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Yeah, my girlfriend takes collect calls from the road<BR>And it doesn't seem to matter that I'm lacking in the bulge<BR>She laughs at my dumb jokes when no one does<BR>She brings me mexican food from Sombrero's just because<BR>                 <I>-Blink 182</I>||||reg||12
